 "source": "ATLAS-style LO+PS at 13.6 TeV: LO gg -> l+l-H events of ggxy_ggZH (POWHEG-BOX-V2, bornonly), PDF4LHC21, dynamic scale mu_R = mu_F = H_T = m_T(H) + p_T(l1) + p_T(l2) (dynscale 3), 15 < m_ll < 150 GeV, showered with Pythia 8 (A14 as the ATLAS job options set it, the ATLAS base settings and the ATLAS POWHEG veto at SCALUP = m_ZH); set atlas13600, runs events-lo and table-lo-atlas",
 "target": "NLO+PS at 13.6 TeV: the production NLO events (Born suppression 250 GeV, PDF4LHC21 nominal weight), showered with the same A14 settings, the ATLAS base settings and the NLO POWHEG veto; set atlas13600, run table-nlo-a14; the variations use the target's scale weights",
 "objects": "Z and H: the last copies of the bosons in the event record (Z from its decay leptons' parent); jets: anti-kT R = 0.4 from all stable particles except the descendants of the Z and the Higgs boson",
 "source_events_in_window": 500000,
 "target_events_in_window": 500000,
 "validity": "shape weights for samples defined as the source; outside that definition untested.  The paper's reweighting section gives the tests (STXS fractions, distributions, split-sample stability) and their outcome; a vetoed LO+PS sample lacks events with a jet harder than m_ZH, which no weight recovers.",
 "classifier": {
  "settings": {
   "learning_rate": 0.05,
   "max_iter": 400,
   "max_leaf_nodes": 31,
   "min_samples_leaf": 100,
   "l2_regularization": 1.0,
   "early_stopping": true,
   "validation_fraction": 0.2,
   "n_iter_no_change": 20,
   "random_state": 1
  },
  "training": "all source events vs all target events in the window, balanced classes, target events with their weights (negative weights set to zero)",
  "input_dtype": "float32",
  "thresholds": "each tree threshold stored as the largest float32 value not above the trained one, so that float32 inputs take the same branches in ONNX as in scikit-learn",
  "output": "'probabilities'[:, 1] = p (probability of NLO+PS)",
  "weight": "w = p / (1 - p) / c, with c the mean of p / (1 - p) over the source events in the window (below, per model and variation); events outside 15 < m_ll < 150 GeV: weight 1; for another sample, renormalise to mean 1 over its events in the window",
